\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Mean $\mu $s\ per traced 32-key call, on the path of the owner flight that finished last. Pre-flight: call start to the first flight's admission. Group gap: delay until the last flight's admission. Submit wait: admission to request submission. Flight: submission to completion. Owners is the mean number of owner flights per call. The traced calls are the first calls after the trace was armed.}}{12}{table.caption.20}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:readmany}{{9}{12}{Mean \us \ per traced 32-key call, on the path of the owner flight that finished last. Pre-flight: call start to the first flight's admission. Group gap: delay until the last flight's admission. Submit wait: admission to request submission. Flight: submission to completion. Owners is the mean number of owner flights per call. The traced calls are the first calls after the trace was armed}{table.caption.20}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Device writes of a 1~KiB put at concurrency 16 (synchronous tier; Native uses its value-WAL barrier). Writes and KiB per put are \texttt  {/proc/diskstats} deltas of the Local SSD between the measurement gates, divided by successful puts. The owners columns use the five storage hosts (the coordinator\textquoteright s own SSD for Native); the all-hosts column adds the coordinator. They include journal, metadata and any other I/O on the device. Flushes are device flush requests. One repetition.}}{13}{table.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:writes}{{10}{13}{Device writes of a 1~KiB put at concurrency 16 (synchronous tier; Native uses its value-WAL barrier). Writes and KiB per put are \texttt {/proc/diskstats} deltas of the Local SSD between the measurement gates, divided by successful puts. The owners columns use the five storage hosts (the coordinator\textquoteright s own SSD for Native); the all-hosts column adds the coordinator. They include journal, metadata and any other I/O on the device. Flushes are device flush requests. One repetition}{table.caption.21}{}}
